## Directory Structure
<!-- cs: Adresářová struktura -->

```
doc/project-progress/
├── GLOSSARY.md
├── DECISIONS.md
├── brief.md
├── spec.md
├── roadmap.md
└── epic-010-name/
    ├── plan.md
    ├── report.md
    └── task-010-name/
        ├── spec.md         # Task Specification + Context Bundle
        ├── dod.md          # Definition of Done checklist
        ├── report.md       # Task Report (Coder)
        └── review.md       # Task Review (Reviewer) — APPROVE / REQUEST CHANGES
```

Numbering in steps of 10 — insertion: `epic-015-name/` between `epic-010` and `epic-020`.
<!-- cs: Číslování po 10 — vkládání: epic-015-name/ mezi epic-010 a epic-020. -->

## File Header (YAML front matter)
<!-- cs: Záhlaví souboru (YAML front matter) -->

Every APM document **must** start with this front matter:
<!-- cs: Každý APM dokument musí začínat tímto front matter: -->

```yaml
---
apm_category: task-spec         # see Document Types table above
apm_ref: E010.T020              # E010 = epic ref; E010.T020 = task ref
apm_level: task                 # project | epic | task
created_by: Planner             # Planner | Coder | Reviewer | Human
model: <model-id>               # actual model used (assigned per 000-model-policy.mdc); omit if Human
template_version: v1.1.0        # from .cursor/TEMPLATE_VERSION, read once at document creation
intended_for: Coder             # Planner | Coder | Reviewer | Human | All
created_at: 2026-05-08
updated_at: 2026-05-08
---
```

`template_version` (the `version:` line of `.cursor/TEMPLATE_VERSION`, read once at
creation) lets a later audit tell which rule/DoD conventions a document came from. Omit
only for `brief.md` (Human input).
<!-- cs: template_version (řádek version: v .cursor/TEMPLATE_VERSION) umožní pozdějšímu
     auditu vědět, ze kterých konvencí dokument vycházel. Vynech jen u brief.md. -->

## Task Specification — required sections
<!-- cs: Task Specification — povinné sekce -->

1. **Goal** — what to build (1–3 sentences)
2. **Inputs** — files to read, APIs to call, data provided
3. **Outputs** — files to create/modify, interfaces to expose
4. **Context Bundle** — relevant existing files; files NOT to modify; interfaces from prior Tasks
5. **Dependencies** — which Tasks must be completed first
6. **Test Specification** — what tests to write; happy path + edge cases
7. **Definition of Done** — checklist (→ also written to `dod.md`)
8. **Recommended Coder model** — names the **Coder role** at the Task's **band**
   (`low`/`medium`/`high`, see `000-model-policy.mdc`). Actual models are assigned per
   `000-model-policy.mdc`.

## Definition of Ready (DoR) — Task spec quality gate
<!-- cs: Definition of Ready (DoR) — brána kvality zadání tasku -->

The Planner's output is the quality gate for everything the Coder does — a vague spec
guarantees a failed Task. A Task may be handed to a Coder **only** when its `spec.md`
passes this checklist (the counterpart of the Definition of Done):
<!-- cs: Výstup Plannera je brána kvality. Vágní spec = selhaný task. Task smí dostat Coder
     jen když jeho spec.md projde tímto checklistem (protějšek Definition of Done): -->

- [ ] **Goal** is concrete and measurable (not "improve X").
- [ ] **Outputs** name exact files/interfaces to create or change.
- [ ] **Context Bundle** lists files to read AND files NOT to modify.
- [ ] **Dependencies** are listed and already completed (or none).
- [ ] **Test Specification** names happy path + ≥1 edge + ≥1 error case.
- [ ] **Definition of Done** is verifiable (each item maps to a checkable artifact).
- [ ] **Recommended Coder model** names the Coder role at the Task's band; models are
  assigned per `000-model-policy.mdc`.
- [ ] Task is independently implementable and testable in isolation.

<!-- cs: Goal měřitelný; Outputs konkrétní; Context Bundle úplný (číst i NEsahat);
     závislosti hotové; testy pojmenované (happy/edge/error); DoD ověřitelné;
     model z 000-model-policy.mdc; task nezávisle implementovatelný a testovatelný. -->

The DoR is checked at the **FE.2 Human review** of the Epic Plan. If a Task fails DoR,
the Planner fixes the spec before any Coder starts.
<!-- cs: DoR se kontroluje při FE.2 (Human review plánu epiky). Když task neprojde,
     Planner opraví spec dřív, než začne Coder. -->

## Epic type: spike
<!-- cs: Typ epiky: spike -->

A **spike** answers a question ("which of A/B is faster/cheaper/simpler?") instead of
shipping a feature, on a `spike/<desc>` branch (`020-git.mdc`). Differences from a normal
Epic:
<!-- cs: Spike odpovídá na otázku, ne dodává feature, na větvi spike/<desc>. Rozdíly od
     normální epiky: -->

- **DoR** names metric(s)/dataset/candidates to compare, not a feature Goal.
- **Outputs**: a results table/CSV + short `README.md` — not necessarily production code.
- **Tests** cover only the measurement tool itself; candidates being compared are exempt
  from normal coverage rules.
- **DoD**: metrics filled in **and** an ADR recording the choice and why.
- **Reviewer** checks **reproducibility**, not code quality.
- **Stopping is a Human decision made with the Planner** — never an automatic threshold;
  the Planner may flag "within noise" as input, it does not stop the spike itself.
<!-- cs: DoR jmenuje metriky/dataset/kandidáty, ne cíl. Výstupy: tabulka/CSV + README.md.
     Testy jen pro měřicí nástroj. DoD: metriky + ADR. Reviewer posuzuje
     reprodukovatelnost. Ukončení je rozhodnutí Humana s Plannerem — nikdy automatický
     práh. -->

## Architectural decisions → ADR bridge
<!-- cs: Architektonická rozhodnutí → most na ADR -->

A significant decision recorded in a Task/Epic Report must not stay buried there. When a
decision **affects structure, dependencies, interfaces, or cross-task constraints**,
promote it to an ADR in `doc/architecture/decisions/ADR-NNN-title.md` (see
`060-project-structure.mdc`), and link the ADR from the report.
<!-- cs: Významné rozhodnutí z reportu nesmí zůstat pohřbené. Pokud ovlivňuje strukturu,
     závislosti, rozhraní nebo omezení napříč tasky, povyš ho na ADR v
     doc/architecture/decisions/ a z reportu na něj odkaž. -->

- Coder: during a Task, if such a decision is made → create/append the ADR and reference it.
  <!-- cs: Coder: vznikne-li takové rozhodnutí, vytvoř/doplň ADR a odkaž na něj. -->
- Reviewer: flag any architectural decision in the diff/report that lacks an ADR.
  <!-- cs: Reviewer: označ architektonické rozhodnutí v diffu/reportu, které nemá ADR. -->
- Planner: at Epic close, ensure new ADRs are consistent with `spec.md`.
  <!-- cs: Planner: při uzávěrce epiky ověř, že nové ADR jsou v souladu se spec.md. -->

## Coder — doc/ Write Permission
<!-- cs: Coder — oprávnění k zápisu do doc/ -->

Task specs and epic plans often state **"Do NOT modify `doc/**`"** in their Context Bundle.
This constraint means: do not touch **other tasks'** `spec.md`/`dod.md`, the epic `plan.md`,
project `spec.md`, `roadmap.md`, or `doc/architecture/` ADRs.

It does **NOT** prevent — and in fact **requires** — Coder to:

- Create `report.md` in the **current task's own directory** (e.g. `task-010-foo/report.md`)
- Fill checkboxes in the **current task's own `dod.md`**

<!-- cs: "Do NOT modify doc/**" v Context Bundle znamená: nesahej na spec, plan, roadmap, ADRs
     a cizí taskové soubory. Coder MUSÍ zapsat report.md a vyplnit dod.md v adresáři svého tasku. -->

## Coder — Task Report
<!-- cs: Coder — Task Report -->

Write `task-NNN/report.md` prose in `<communication-language>` (see `000-communication-language.mdc`). This section defines structure in **English**; rendered `##`/`###` headings must follow the mapping table when `<lang-code>` ≠ `en`.
<!-- cs: Prostý text reportu piš v <communication-language>. Tato sekce je anglicky; nadpisy v reportu musí odpovídat tabulce mapping pro cs (ne en). -->

This is the **full (`high`-band) report**. `medium`/`low` Tasks use a shorter tier, and
the Human gate (FT.7) below is not opened for every Task — see the band table in
`090-apm-orchestration.mdc`.
<!-- cs: Tohle je plný report pro pásmo high. medium/low mají kratší úroveň a brána FT.7 se
     neotevírá po každém tasku — viz tabulka pásem v 090-apm-orchestration.mdc. -->

### Required content (ordered `##` sections)
<!-- cs: Povinný obsah (pořadí sekcí ##) -->

| # | Section (English) | Czech (`cs`) `##` heading in `report.md` |
|---|-------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| 1 | What was implemented | `## Co bylo implementováno` |
| 2 | Inputs and outputs | `## Vstupy a výstupy` |
| 3 | Methods and decisions | `## Použité metody a rozhodnutí` |
| 4 | Deviations from spec.md | `## Odchylky od spec.md` |
| 5 | Code references | `## Reference do kódu` |
| 6 | Regression test results | `## Výsledek regresního testu` |
| 7 | Definition of Done | `## Definition of Done` |

When `<lang-code>` = `en`, use the English phrase as the `##` heading (e.g. `## What was implemented`). Optional follow-ups: extra `##` (e.g. *Notes*) only if needed; title in `<communication-language>`.
<!-- cs: Pro `en` použij anglický název z prvního sloupce tabulky jako `##` nadpis. Volitelné `##` (např. poznámky) jen pokud dává smysl; titulek v <communication-language>. -->

1. **What was implemented** — short summary (bullets preferred).
2. **Inputs and outputs** — read / created / changed / not touched lists.
3. **Methods and decisions** — key architecture and implementation choices.
4. **Deviations from spec.md** — `—` if none; otherwise, for each deviation: what, why,
   impact. The Reviewer treats an undisclosed deviation found in the diff as a finding.
5. **Code references** — files, notable symbols, line ranges.
6. **Regression test results** — ✅ all pass / ❌ failures, commands, exit codes, counts.
7. **Definition of Done** — short summary + link to `dod.md` (do not duplicate the full checklist).

### Mandatory Markdown layout (task `report.md`)
<!-- cs: Povinné Markdown rozložení (task report.md) -->

- Between top-level `##` sections, optional `---` **only** if it improves scanability (avoid spamming rules).
  <!-- cs: Mezi sekcemi ## volitelně --- jen pro čitelnost. -->

- **What was implemented:** use bullets; avoid one continuous paragraph longer than ~4 sentences.
  <!-- cs: Co bylo implementováno: odrážky; žádný mega-odstavec. -->

- **Inputs and outputs:** use `###` subsections; **one repo path per bullet**, always in backticks. For `cs`: `### Přečteno`, `### Vytvořeno`, `### Změněno`, `### Nedotčeno (Context Bundle)`. For `en`: `### Read`, `### Created`, `### Changed`, `### Not modified (Context Bundle)`.
  <!-- cs: Vstupy/výstupy: podsekce ###; jedna cesta na řádek v backticks. -->

- **Methods and decisions:** split themes: either separate `### Topic` blocks or bullets with a **bold** lead-in line followed by a short paragraph; do not merge unrelated topics in one bullet.
  <!-- cs: Metody: odděl témata (### nebo tučný úvod); neslučuj nesouvisející body. -->

- **Code references:** include a **Markdown table**: `| File | Lines | Summary |` (lines = range such as `1-42`). Put function/class names in Summary when useful.
  <!-- cs: Reference: tabulka Soubor | Řádky | Shrnutí. -->

- **Regression test results:** use a **table** (`| Command / scope | Result | Notes |`) or clearly structured bullets with command, outcome, and exit code (state **0 tests** / pytest exit **5** when applicable).
  <!-- cs: Regrese: tabulka nebo jasné odrážky včetně exit kódů. -->

- **Definition of Done:** one short paragraph + `[dod.md](dod.md)` link.
  <!-- cs: DoD: krátce + odkaz na dod.md. -->

❌ One bullet with comma-separated paths for “created” files.  
✅ One path per line under `### Created` / `### Vytvořeno`.

## Security guard
<!-- cs: Bezpečnostní zábrany -->

- No `git commit/push` without explicit Human approval.
  <!-- cs: Žádný git commit/push bez explicitního souhlasu člověka. -->
- No database migrations without Human approval.
  <!-- cs: Žádné DB migrace bez souhlasu člověka. -->
- No destructive file operations without confirmation.
  <!-- cs: Žádné destruktivní operace se soubory bez potvrzení. -->
